  "analysis": "Bacterial meningitis in children can lead to several developmental complications due to the inflammation and potential damage to the central nervous system. Among these, hearing loss is the most common complication. This is because the infection and subsequent inflammation can affect the cochlea or auditory nerve, leading to sensorineural hearing loss. While other complications such as residual epilepsy, mental retardation, hydrocephalus, and visual defects can occur, they are less frequent compared to hearing loss. The consensus in medical literature supports hearing loss as the most prevalent developmental issue following bacterial meningitis in the pediatric population.",
